ur direct call is fine.\n\nAlso, should I verify that the hook actually raises on error status? E.g., build a fake response with `raise_for_status` that raises HTTPError, and assert the hook propagates it. That's extra but nice:\n\n```python\n    failing = Mock()\n    failing.raise_for_status.side_effect = HTTPError(\"boom\")\n    with pytest.raises(HTTPError):\n        session.hooks[\"response\"][0](failing)\n```\n\nEh, that's testing the lambda trivially. The `assert_called_once_with` check is enough. Keep it simple.\n\nNow \u2014 cleanup/state pollution: no global state modified except monkeypatch (auto-restored). Sessions are local. No network. Good.\n\nLet me also double check line coverage mapping:\n\n- Test 1 (defaults): lines 26, 27(T), 28, 29(T), 30(T), 31, 36, 37, 38, 39. \u2713\n- Test 2 (no hooks, no retry): 26, 27(F), 29(F), 39. \u2713\n- Test 3 (retry=3): 26, 27(T), 28, 29(T), 30(F), 32(T), 33, 36, 37, 38, 39. \u2713\n- Test 4 (Retry instance): 26, 27(T), 28, 29(T), 30(F), 32(F), 34(F), 36, 37, 38, 39. \u2713\n- Test 5 (invalid): 26, 27(T), 28, 29(T), 30(F), 32(F), 34(T), 35. \u2713 (39 not reached due to exception \u2014 fine, covered elsewhere.)\n\nAll lines 26-39 covered: 26\u2713, 27\u2713(both), 28\u2713, 29\u2713(both), 30\u2713(both), 31\u2713, 32\u2713(both), 33\u2713, 34\u2713(both), 35\u2713, 36\u2713, 37\u2713, 38\u2713, 39\u2713. \n\nNow, before finalizing, let me use get_info to check the actual function. I'll call get_info(\"build_requests_session\"). Possibly also get_info(\"helpers\") or something. The tool takes a name like 'f' or 'C.foo'. Let me call it with \"build_requests_session\".\n\nI should make the independent calls in the same block. I could call get_info for \"build_requests_session\" and maybe \"HTTPAdapter\" \u2014 but HTTPAdapter is from requests, probably not in the tool's scope. Let me just call for build_requests_session first, and maybe also \"Retry\" \u2014 no. Just one call, then write the tests.\n\nActually, the instruction says to use get_info \"as necessary\". One call to confirm the function's module/behavior is reasonable. Let me do it.\n\nAfter getting info, write the final test script.\n\nLet me draft the final test file:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Tests for semantic_release.helpers.build_requests_session.\"\"\"\n\nfrom unittest.mock import Mock\n\nimport pytest\nfrom requests import Session\nfrom requests.adapters import HTTPAdapter\nfrom requests.packages.urllib3.util.retry import Retry\n\nfrom semantic_release.helpers import build_requests_session\n\n\ndef test_build_requests_session_defaults():\n    \"\"\"Default call installs the raise_for_status hook and a default Retry adapter.\"\"\"\n    session = build_requests_session()\n\n    assert isinstance(session, Session)\n\n    # A raise_for_status response hook must have been installed.\n    assert \"response\" in session.hooks\n    assert len(session.hooks[\"response\"]) == 1\n    mock_response = Mock()\n    session.hooks[\"response\"][0](mock_response)\n    mock_response.raise_for_status.assert_called_once_with()\n\n    # A default Retry configuration must be mounted on both schemes,\n    # using one single shared adapter instance.\n    http_adapter = session.get_adapter(\"http://example.com/path\")\n    https_adapter = session.get_adapter(\"https://example.com/path\")\n    assert isinstance(http_adapter, HTTPAdapter)\n    assert http_adapter is https_adapter\n    assert isinstance(http_adapter.max_retries, Retry)\n    assert http_adapter.max_retries.total == Retry().total\n\n\ndef test_build_requests_session_no_hook_no_retry(monkeypatch):\n    \"\"\"raise_for_status=False and retry=False install neither hook nor adapter.\"\"\"\n    constructed = []\n    real_http_adapter = HTTPAdapter\n\n    def recording_http_adapter(*args, **kwargs):\n        constructed.append(kwargs)\n        return real_http_adapter(*args, **kwargs)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        \"semantic_release.helpers.HTTPAdapter\", recording_http_adapter\n    )\n\n    session = build_requests_session(raise_for_status=False, retry=False)\n\n    assert isinstance(session, Session)\n    # No raise_for_status hook was installed.\n    assert session.hooks == {\"response\": []}\n    # No extra adapter was built/mounted by build_requests_session.\n    assert constructed == []\n    # The mounted adapters are the plain Session defaults (distinct instances).\n    assert session.get_adapter(\"http://example.com\") is not session.get_adapter(\n        \"https://example.com\"\n    )\n\n\ndef test_build_requests_session_retry_as_int():\n    \"\"\"An integer retry is converted into a Retry with that total.\"\"\"\n    session = build_requests_session(retry=3)\n\n    adapter = session.get_adapter(\"https://example.com/path\")\n    assert isinstance(adapter, HTTPAdapter)\n    assert isinstance(adapter.max_retries, Retry)\n    assert adapter.max_retries.total == 3\n    # The same adapter instance serves both http and https.\n    assert session.get_adapter(\"http://example.com/path\") is adapter\n\n\ndef test_build_requests_session_retry_as_retry_instance():\n    \"\"\"A Retry instance is used as-is for the mounted adapter.\"\"\"\n    retry = Retry(total=7, status=2)\n    session = build_requests_session(retry=retry)\n\n    adapter = session.get_adapter(\"https://example.com/path\")\n    assert isinstance(adapter, HTTPAdapter)\n    assert adapter.max_retries.total == 7\n    assert adapter.max_retries.status == 2\n    assert session.get_adapter(\"http://example.com/path\") is adapter\n\n\ndef test_build_requests_session_invalid_retry_raises():\n    \"\"\"Any other retry value is rejected with a ValueError.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(\n        ValueError, match=r\"retry should be a bool, int or Retry instance\\.\"\n    ):\n        build_requests_session(retry=\"not-a-retry\")\n```\n\nWait \u2014 in test 2, `session.hooks == {\"response\": []}`: hmm, actually let me double-check `default_hooks`. requests/sessions.py:\n\n```python\nHOOK