pond ONLY with the Python code enclosed in backticks, without any explanation.\" So my final response should be just the code block. But I already made tool calls with some text \u2014 that's fine; the final answer must be only code. Actually the instruction says respond ONLY with the Python code \u2014 I'll keep the final message to just the code block.\n\nLet me write it:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Unit tests for semantic_release.helpers.build_requests_session.\"\"\"\n\nfrom unittest.mock import Mock\n\nimport pytest\nfrom requests import Session\nfrom requests.adapters import HTTPAdapter\nfrom requests.packages.urllib3.util.retry import Retry\n\nfrom semantic_release.helpers import build_requests_session\n\n\ndef test_build_requests_session_defaults():\n    \"\"\"Default arguments install the raise_for_status hook and a default Retry adapter.\"\"\"\n    session = build_requests_session()\n\n    assert isinstance(session, Session)\n\n    # raise_for_status=True installs a single \"response\" hook that calls\n    # raise_for_status() on the response it receives.\n    assert \"response\" in session.hooks\n    assert len(session.hooks[\"response\"]) == 1\n    mock_response = Mock()\n    session.hooks[\"response\"][0](mock_response)\n    mock_response.raise_for_status.assert_called_once_with()\n\n    # retry=True mounts one shared HTTPAdapter with a default Retry\n    # configuration on both the http:// and https:// prefixes.\n    http_adapter = session.get_adapter(\"http://example.com/path\")\n    https_adapter = session.get_adapter(\"https://example.com/path\")\n    assert isinstance(http_adapter, HTTPAdapter)\n    assert http_adapter is https_adapter\n    assert isinstance(http_adapter.max_retries, Retry)\n    assert http_adapter.max_retries.total == Retry().total\n\n\ndef test_build_requests_session_disabled(monkeypatch):\n    \"\"\"raise_for_status=False and retry=False install neither hook nor adapter.\"\"\"\n    constructed = []\n    real_http_adapter = HTTPAdapter\n\n    def recording_http_adapter(*args, **kwargs):\n        constructed.append(kwargs)\n        return real_http_adapter(*args, **kwargs)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        \"semantic_release.helpers.HTTPAdapter\", recording_http_adapter\n    )\n\n    session = build_requests_session(raise_for_status=False, retry=False)\n\n    assert isinstance(session, Session)\n    # No raise_for_status hook was installed.\n    assert session.hooks == {\"response\": []}\n    # build_requests_session did not build (nor mount) any extra adapter.\n    assert constructed == []\n    # Only the plain Session defaults remain: two distinct adapter instances.\n    http_adapter = session.get_adapter(\"http://example.com\")\n    https_adapter = session.get_adapter(\"https://example.com\")\n    assert isinstance(http_adapter, HTTPAdapter)\n    assert http_adapter is not https_adapter\n\n\ndef test_build_requests_session_retry_as_int():\n    \"\"\"An integer retry is converted into a Retry with that total.\"\"\"\n    session = build_requests_session(retry=3)\n\n    adapter = session.get_adapter(\"https://example.com/path\")\n    assert isinstance(adapter, HTTPAdapter)\n    assert isinstance(adapter.max_retries, Retry)\n    assert adapter.max_retries.total == 3\n    # The same adapter instance serves both http and https.\n    assert session.get_adapter(\"http://example.com/path\") is adapter\n\n\ndef test_build_requests_session_retry_as_retry_instance():\n    \"\"\"A Retry instance is handed to the mounted adapter unchanged.\"\"\"\n    retry = Retry(total=7)\n    session = build_requests_session(retry=retry)\n\n    adapter = session.get_adapter(\"https://example.com/path\")\n    assert isinstance(adapter, HTTPAdapter)\n    assert adapter.max_retries is retry\n    assert adapter.max_retries.total == 7\n    assert session.get_adapter(\"http://example.com/path\") is adapter\n\n\ndef test_build_requests_session_invalid_retry_raises():\n    \"\"\"Any other retry type is rejected with a ValueError.\"\"\"\n    with pytest.raises(\n        ValueError, match=r\"retry should be a bool, int or Retry instance\\.\"\n    ):\n        build_requests_session(retry=\"not-a-retry\")\n```\n\nWait \u2014 in test 4, `adapter.max_retries is retry`: confirmed by get_info that requests does `Retry.from_int(max_retries)` and urllib3's from_int returns Retry instances unchanged. \u2713 Safe.\n\nHmm, but one thing: in test 4, should I also assert `adapter.max_retries.total == 7`? Yes, included.\n\nAlso, in test 1, `http_adapter.max_retries.total == Retry().total` \u2014 with this requests version, `HTTPAdapter(max_retries=Retry())` \u2192 from_int returns the Retry() instance \u2192 total = Retry().total. \u2713\n\nOne more consideration for test 2: `session.hooks == {\"response\": []}` \u2014 confirmed default_hooks. \u2713\n\nAlso, is there any chance `build_requests_session` with retry=False still triggers HTTPAdapter construction through Session()? Session() constructs HTTPAdapter via requests.sessions' import \u2014 not the patched name. \u2713 constructed stays []. \u2713\n\nCoverage re-check with the confirmed source:\n\nLines (1-indexed per snippet): 26 session=Session() \u2014 all tests. 27 if raise_for_status \u2014 T (tests 1,3,4,5), F (test 2). 28 hooks assignment \u2014 tests 1,3,4,5. 29 if retry \u2014 T (1,3,4,5), F (2). 30 isinstance bool \u2014 T (1), F (3,4,5). 31 retry=Retry() \u2014 test 1. 32 elif isinstance int \u2014 T (3), F (4,5). 33 Retry(retry) \u2014 test 3. 34 elif not isinstance Retry \u2014 T (5), F (4). 35 raise \u2014 test 5. 36 adapter=HTTPAdapter \u2014 1,3,4. 37,38 mount \u2014 1,3,4. 39 return \u2014 1,2,3,4. Full coverage of lines 26-39 and all branches. \u2713\n\nThe monkeypatch in test 2 auto-cleans. No other global state. No network. \u2713\n\nI think this is solid. One last thought: should I use `pytest.raises` match without escaping? `match=r\"retry should be a bool, int or Retry instance\\.\"` \u2014 re.search against the string representation of the exception. The message contains that exact text. \u2713\n\nAlso, minor: in test 2, defining `recording_http_adapter` closure referencing `real_http_adapter` \u2014 fine.\n\nAlso, should tests close sessions? `session.close()` \u2014 adapters hold pool managers but no connections opened; closing is harmless and good hygiene. I could add `session.close()` at the end of each test... It's not strictly needed (no requests made), but \"clean up\" spirit. I'll skip \u2014 no connections were opened; Session.close() would be noise. Actually, adding close() is cheap and shows diligence. Hmm, keep the code clean; no network resources were created. Skip.\n\nFinal answer: just the code block.",
